# PNG SIZES GUIDE

### These are the sprite & *.png image sizes guide for adding in or modifying to formulate your unqiue experienced game play. Setting a /Campaigns/ folder to store the campaign names as folders to then store the /Sprites/ internal data so you can quickly swap between different campaigns by sprite change. TOAST & TOAST Boss Sim are designed to use the /Sprites/ folder to expand past the inital failsafe of text, poly, simple geomtry for the entire in-game elements incuding: usable objects, findable objects, characters, enemies, NPCs, etc.


### Each sectional header contains Range of allowed .png sizes for what is specially named; the Default size (also marked by wrapping '*' in the list); the name scheme for what is speically named; the folder in which the png for what is specially named will be found.


#### {sprite_type} [min-max range: {{min_range} - {max_range}}; Default: {default_size};] ({naming_scheme [if plain text & not '{' '}' wrapped, a specific name is looked for]} == {naming_scheme [if there are two naming_schemes listed, this second one is the fallback]}) /{directory_location}/
---




# TOAST Engine
---

## Splash Screen [min-max range: {800x800 - 1200x930}; Default: 1200x930;] (splash_screen.png == {ui_element}_{ui_location}.png) /Sprites/
 - 1221x936 (technically allowed)
 - *1200x930 (inital starting size)*
 - 800x800 (padded starting size)
 - 640x640 (big credit)
 - 400x400 (small credit)
 - 250x250 (technically allowed)

## DIY Character [min-max range: {1x1 - 1042x1042}; Default: 128x128;] ({character-name}_{starting-facing-direction}.png) /Sprites/Characters/
 - 1042x1024 (technically allowed)
 - 840x840 (breaks collisions)
 - 512x512 (over-sized)
 - 256x256 (chonky)
 - *128x128 (best fit)*
 - 84x84 (prefered)
 - 64x64 (usable)
 - 48x48 (under-sized)
 - 67-x67- (???)


## Interactive Objects [min-max range: {1x1 - 1042x1042}; Default: 256x256;] ({objectname}.png) /Sprites/
 - 1024x1024 (mega-boss sized)
 - 420x420 (loud)
 - *256x256 (best fit)*
 - 128x128 (prefered)
 - 84x84 (usable)
 - 83-x83- (???)


## Directional Arrows [min-max range: {1x1 - 1042x1042}; Default: 48x48;] ({directionphrase}_arrow.png) /Sprites/
 - 84x84 (currently used for edges [special case])
 - 73x73 (currently used for corners [special case])
 - 52x52 (breaks past program edge)
 - 50x50 (largest possible)
 - *48x48 (best fit)*
 - 40x40 (prefered)
 - 32x32 (usable)
 - 28x28 (under-sized)
 - 20x20 (decently small)
 - 16x16 (crazy small)
 - 10x10 (smallest viewable)
 - 5x5 (smallest possible)
 - 4x4 (debatable if usable)
 - 1x2 (a line)
 - 1x1 (technically allowed)

